{
  "0": "Replace the current readout with a normalized exponential pooling of nonpadding GRU states using decay 0.9. Use causal prefix pooling at every supervised timestep and the identical final-prefix readout at inference. Compared with the previously tested decay 0.8, the longer aggregation horizon may stabilize interests across noisy recent interactions. Preserve history selection, embeddings, GRU topology, scoring, loss and optimizer; update the predictor writer consistently.",
  "1": "Add a deterministic causal repetition feature by multiplying each input item embedding by 1 + 0.1*min(log1p(c), log(4)), where c counts earlier occurrences of that item within the supplied input prefix. Leave padding zero and candidate embeddings unchanged. This bounded emphasis may help the GRU recognize repeated interests without adding embedding tables or a separate scorer. Preserve context selection, GRU topology, readout, loss and optimizer; reproduce the feature in the predictor writer.",
  "2": "Halve the current initial learning rate while preserving the optimizer, scheduler shape and minimum-to-initial learning-rate ratio. Smaller updates may stabilize training under the existing hard-negative-weighted loss and improve validation HR@10. Keep batch size, dropout, weight decay, model, loss, seed 42, evaluation, early stopping and the 200-epoch cap unchanged.",
  "3": "Set the maximum causal context length to 64 for training and inference, retaining the latest interactions in chronological order with the existing padding convention. Shorter context may reduce stale-interest interference and recurrent computation while retaining useful recent behavior. Preserve feature definitions, embeddings, GRU topology, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer. Save the context length in metadata and update the predictor writer consistently. Retain all four dataset routes and one model per category."
}
